.TH ACC-PKG 1 2026-10-22 "ACC" "ACC Manual"
.SH NAME
acc-pkg \- build, sign, publish, install and query ACC role packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acc-pkg
.RB [ \-\-quiet ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acc-pkg
is the toolchain for ACC role packages (\fI.accpkg\fR): signed archives
carrying roles, skills, MCP definitions, evals and golden prompts.
Its query verbs are modelled on
.BR rpm (8)
(\fBqf\fR, \fBql\fR, \fBqi\fR, \fBqv\fR) and its build and scaffold verbs on
.BR rpmbuild (8).
.PP
Installation verifies the package signature before anything is unpacked:
keypair mode with a cosign public key (\fB\-\-key\fR), or keyless mode
against a Sigstore bundle (\fB\-\-issuer\fR, \fB\-\-subject\fR).
An unsigned package is refused unless \fB\-\-allow\-unsigned\fR is given,
which is logged as an audit event.
An Enterprise Contract policy, when present, is evaluated before the install
is committed.
.PP
.B acc-pkg
never prompts; it is built for CI and automation.
It is the package toolchain;
.BR acc-cli (1)
drives a running collective.
.SH OPTIONS
These sit before the command and apply to every command.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress non-error standard output.
The \fB\-\-allow\-unsigned\fR audit line still prints.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON for the commands that produce data.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
