.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACC_PACKAGES_ROOT
Where packages are installed and queried (default \fB/var/lib/acc/packages\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_SYSTEM_CATALOG
The system catalog list (default \fB/etc/acc/catalogs.yaml\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_USER_CATALOG
The per-user catalog list (default \fB~/.acc/catalogs.yaml\fR).
.TP
.B COSIGN_PRIVATE_KEY
Private key for keypair signing in \fBpublish\fR when \fB\-\-key\fR is not given.
.TP
.BR SIGSTORE_ID_TOKEN ", " SIGSTORE_OIDC_ISSUER
The OIDC token and issuer for keyless signing; \fBacc\-pkg login\fR reports
whether they are usable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/acc/packages
The installed packages and their registry.
.TP
.I /etc/acc/catalogs.yaml
The catalogs \fBlist \-\-available\fR and the resolver read.
.TP
.I /etc/acc/policy/enterprise\-contract.yaml
The default Enterprise Contract policy for \fBinstall\fR and \fBverify\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
User or argument error: missing file, bad arguments, unsafe path, already installed.
.TP
.B 2
Manifest schema failure, validation or lint errors.
.TP
.B 3
Dependency resolution failure, or an uninstall refused because something
still depends on the package.
.TP
.B 4
Content hash mismatch (tampering or corruption).
.TP
.B 5
Signature missing or rejected.
.TP
.B 6
Enterprise Contract policy violation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
acc\-pkg init my_role \-\-scope @you \-\-domain finance
acc\-pkg validate ./my_role
acc\-pkg build ./my_role \-o dist/my_role.accpkg
acc\-pkg publish dist/my_role.accpkg \-\-catalog\-url https://catalog.example/
acc\-pkg install dist/my_role.accpkg \-\-key cosign.pub
acc\-pkg list \-\-available
acc\-pkg qf \-\-kind role coding_agent    # which package provides a role
acc\-pkg qv                              # re-check every installed hash
.fi
